    "result_text": "There's only one test class, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `displayName` field on the owner response, formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName`:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `displayName` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` (and thus the JSON response) carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` with an expression on `toOwnerDto`, computing `displayName` as `owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName()` from the stored names.\n\nBecause `displayName` is read-only and derived in the mapper, the create flow (`POST /api/owners`) and read flow (`GET /api/owners/{id}`) both return it without changing the persistence model or the OfficeFloor endpoint pipelines. The `AcceptanceTest` (which creates an owner and asserts `$.displayName` == `\"LastName, John\"`) passes, and the full test suite builds green.",
